{
	"_about": [
		"Looks a map opts into (pass 16, LOOKS; src/map_kit/): foliage scattered on natural ground, dressing as hand-made vignettes set against walls, water (ponds, creeks, troughs) and the ground rules all three keep to. No chapter uses any of it.",
		"foliage: kind -> pictures (camera-facing sprites, one picked a plant), height [least, most] in cells, spacing (the least distance between two plants of the kind at density 1), block (the trunk's half width that stops a body; 0 none), wall (how far off a wall it stands), ground (the floors it grows on; missing: natural), near_water (it grows only within that many cells of water).",
		"vignettes: a group of things that belong together, made by hand, set with its back to a wall: id -> themes, where (outside, inside or any), by_door (it wants a door within 4 cells along its wall, never in front of it), size [along the wall, out from it] in whole cells, items: a town prop (prop, at [along, out] from the run's corner at the wall face, solid: a base that blocks, that half wide; scale) or a fixture (box [along, out] half sizes, at, top, side and cap tiles).",
		"themes: the names a dress object may ask for. water: how deep a bed is carved and how its shore is drawn. clear: how far scatter and dressing keep off the way (route), doors, objectives, spawns, roads and other things. budget: how much foliage a map may have."
	],
